/-
# HC Gap L4 -- Front C200: target-line nonzero gives the generator (R765).

R764 moves the source-containment frontier to target-line geometry:

  * prove `j_q(h^4) in target_invariants`;
  * prove `target_invariants <= span {j_q(h^4)}`;
  * keep honest `MatsushimaV56BoundaryData` explicit.

This file proves the linear-algebra compression behind the next attack.  If the
target-invariant subspace is contained in the one-dimensional line generated by
`j_q(h^4)` and has any nonzero class, then the generator of that line is itself
in `target_invariants`.  Therefore the generator-membership half can be
attacked by proving target-line containment plus target nonvanishing.

No target-line theorem, nonvanishing theorem, boundary theorem, or Hodge
conjecture closure is asserted here.
-/

